{"schema_version": "marine_pump_page_layout_v2_1", "parser_version": "marine_pump_pdfplumber_layout_v2_1", "doc_id": "MP005", "document_split": "build_train", "source_family_id": "DESMI", "publisher": "DESMI", "title": "DESMI NSL Monobloc and Spacer Operation and Maintenance Instructions", "source_url": "https://www.desmi.com/media/dx1lnug1/t1542uk.pdf", "source_tier": "A", "pump_type": "centrifugal_pump", "service": "marine_cooling_bilge_ballast_and_fire_service", "applicability_scope": "优先适用于手册列明的NSL船用离心泵应用", "local_file": "data/source_docs/marine_pump/raw/DESMI_NSL_Pump_T1542.pdf", "document_sha256": "B88E454110CFE5FE8E990C701960DA8CBE59F53D48887454502D226A25DBCB7A", "pdf_page_number": 60, "page_width": 595.44, "page_height": 841.68, "page_text": "                                                                                  \n                                                                                  \n                                                                                  \n          TROUBLESHOOTING                                                         \n                                                                                  \n                                                                                  \n                                                                                  \n          7. TROUBLESHOOTING                                                      \n                                                                                  \n                                                                                  \n          It is often difficult to calculate a manometric delivery head in advance. It is, however, decisively\n          important to the quantity of liquid delivered.                          \n                                                                                  \n          A considerably smaller delivery head than expected will increase the quantity of liquid delivered,\n                                                                                  \n          causing increased power consumption and perhaps cavitation in pump and piping. In the pump,\n          the impeller may show signs of heavy erosion caused by cavitation (corrosion) which may at times\n                                                                                  \n          render an impeller unfit for use in a very short time. Similar erosions also occur in pipe bends and\n          valves elsewhere in the piping system.                                  \n                                                                                  \n          Therefore, after start-up, it is necessary to check either the quantity of liquid delivered or the power\n          consumption of the pump e.g. by measuring the current intensity of the connected motor. Together\n                                                                                  \n          with a reading of the differential pressure, the quantity of water delivered can be determined\n          against the characteristics of the pump.                                \n                                                                                  \n          If the pump does not function as intended, please proceed according to the fault-finding list. Bear\n                                                                                  \n          in mind, though, that the pump was carefully checked and tested at the factory and that the\n          majority of faults stem from the piping system.                         \n                                                                                  \n                                                                                  \n                FAULT               CAUSE                  REMEDY                 \n                                                                                  \n                                                   Change direction of rotation to\n                            1. Wrong direction of rotation clockwise when viewed from shaft\n                                                   end (the direction of the arrow)\n                                                                                  \n                                                   Clean or replace the piping    \n                            2. Piping system is choked                            \n                                                   system                         \n                            3. The pump is choked  Clean the pump                 \n            The pump has no or                                                    \n            too low capacity 4. Suction line leaks                                \n                                                   Find the leakage, repair the fault,\n                            5. Pump takes air      non-return valve not submerged \n                                                   Check data sheet Q/H curve and \n                            6. Suction lift is too high                           \n                                                   NPSH or contact DESMI          \n                            7. Pump and piping system                             \n                                                   As 5                           \n                              wrongly dimensioned                                 \n                                                   Insert orifice plate or check valve\n                            1. Counter-pressure is too low                        \n                                                   / Contact DESMI                \n            The pump uses too 2. The liquid is heavier than                       \n                                                   Contact DESMI                  \n            much power        water                                               \n                                                   Dismantle the pump, remove the \n                            3. Foreign body in pump                               \n                                                   cause                          \n                                                                DESMI Pumping Technology A/S\n                                                                        Tagholm 1 \n                                                                 9400 Nørresundby – Denmark\n                                                                   Tlf. nr.: +45 96 32 81 11\n                                                                     Fax +45 98 17 54 99\n          59                                               E-mail: desmi@desmi.com www.desmi.com", "page_text_sha256": "c29925aa48cc183b307a04fb591b6976ea5b650c1959d45fdfc11d2f73e2096a", "source_language": "en", "source_language_confidence": 1.0, "language_detection_method": "unicode_script_ratio_v1", "printed_page": {"value": "59", "confidence": 1.0, "method": "versioned_manual_override", "bbox": null}, "visual_layout_checked": true, "text_blocks": [{"block_id": "MP005:p0060:b0000", "text": "TROUBLESHOOTING", "bbox": {"x0": 72.024, "top": 42.856, "x1": 182.689, "bottom": 53.896}, "reading_order": 0, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP005:p0060:b0001", "text": "7. TROUBLESHOOTING", "bbox": {"x0": 72.024, "top": 89.396, "x1": 248.648, "bottom": 103.436}, "reading_order": 1, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP005:p0060:b0002", "text": "It is often difficult to calculate a manometric delivery head in advance. It is, however, decisively", "bbox": {"x0": 72.024, "top": 128.218, "x1": 531.862, "bottom": 139.258}, "reading_order": 2, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP005:p0060:b0003", "text": "important to the quantity of liquid delivered.", "bbox": {"x0": 72.024, "top": 147.178, "x1": 281.784, "bottom": 158.218}, "reading_order": 3, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP005:p0060:b0004", "text": "A considerably smaller delivery head than expected will increase the quantity of liquid delivered,", "bbox": {"x0": 72.024, "top": 172.138, "x1": 538.033, "bottom": 183.178}, "reading_order": 4, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP005:p0060:b0005", "text": "causing increased power consumption and perhaps cavitation in pump and piping. In the pump,", "bbox": {"x0": 72.024, "top": 191.098, "x1": 536.278, "bottom": 202.138}, "reading_order": 5, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP005:p0060:b0006", "text": "the impeller may show signs of heavy erosion caused by cavitation (corrosion) which may at times", "bbox": {"x0": 72.024, "top": 210.058, "x1": 548.961, "bottom": 221.098}, "reading_order": 6, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP005:p0060:b0007", "text": "render an impeller unfit for use in a very short time. Similar erosions also occur in pipe bends and", "bbox": {"x0": 72.024, "top": 229.018, "x1": 544.657, "bottom": 240.058}, "reading_order": 7, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP005:p0060:b0008", "text": "valves elsewhere in the piping system.", "bbox": {"x0": 72.024, "top": 248.098, "x1": 259.748, "bottom": 259.138}, "reading_order": 8, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP005:p0060:b0009", "text": "Therefore, after start-up, it is necessary to check either the quantity of liquid delivered or the power", "bbox": {"x0": 72.024, "top": 273.088, "x1": 551.376, "bottom": 284.128}, "reading_order": 9, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP005:p0060:b0010", "text": "consumption of the pump e.g. by measuring the current intensity of the connected motor. Together", "bbox": {"x0": 72.024, "top": 292.048, "x1": 550.63, "bottom": 303.088}, "reading_order": 10, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP005:p0060:b0011", "text": "with a reading of the differential pressure, the quantity of water delivered can be determined", "bbox": {"x0": 72.024, "top": 311.008, "x1": 517.914, "bottom": 322.048}, "reading_order": 11, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP005:p0060:b0012", "text": "against the characteristics of the pump.", "bbox": {"x0": 72.024, "top": 329.968, "x1": 263.424, "bottom": 341.008}, "reading_order": 12, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP005:p0060:b0013", "text": "If the pump does not function as intended, please proceed according to the fault-finding list. Bear", "bbox": {"x0": 72.024, "top": 354.928, "x1": 542.423, "bottom": 365.968}, "reading_order": 13, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP005:p0060:b0014", "text": "in mind, though, that the pump was carefully checked and tested at the factory and that the", "bbox": {"x0": 72.024, "top": 373.888, "x1": 513.646, "bottom": 384.928}, "reading_order": 14, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP005:p0060:b0015", "text": "majority of faults stem from the piping system.", "bbox": {"x0": 72.024, "top": 392.848, "x1": 295.772, "bottom": 403.888}, "reading_order": 15, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP005:p0060:b0016", "text": "FAULT", "bbox": {"x0": 117.62, "top": 429.328, "x1": 153.632, "bottom": 440.368}, "reading_order": 16, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP005:p0060:b0017", "text": "CAUSE", "bbox": {"x0": 261.05, "top": 429.328, "x1": 299.591, "bottom": 440.368}, "reading_order": 17, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP005:p0060:b0018", "text": "REMEDY", "bbox": {"x0": 430.54, "top": 429.328, "x1": 477.604, "bottom": 440.368}, "reading_order": 18, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP005:p0060:b0019", "text": "Change direction of rotation to", "bbox": {"x0": 371.11, "top": 454.428, "x1": 518.56, "bottom": 465.468}, "reading_order": 19, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP005:p0060:b0020", "text": "1. Wrong direction of rotation", "bbox": {"x0": 203.69, "top": 465.108, "x1": 350.059, "bottom": 476.148}, "reading_order": 20, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP005:p0060:b0021", "text": "clockwise when viewed from shaft", "bbox": {"x0": 371.11, "top": 468.108, "x1": 536.876, "bottom": 479.148}, "reading_order": 21, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP005:p0060:b0022", "text": "end (the direction of the arrow)", "bbox": {"x0": 371.11, "top": 481.668, "x1": 521.085, "bottom": 492.708}, "reading_order": 22, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP005:p0060:b0023", "text": "Clean or replace the piping", "bbox": {"x0": 371.11, "top": 502.068, "x1": 502.691, "bottom": 513.108}, "reading_order": 23, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP005:p0060:b0024", "text": "2. Piping system is choked", "bbox": {"x0": 203.69, "top": 505.908, "x1": 339.228, "bottom": 516.948}, "reading_order": 24, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP005:p0060:b0025", "text": "system", "bbox": {"x0": 371.11, "top": 515.748, "x1": 405.974, "bottom": 526.788}, "reading_order": 25, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP005:p0060:b0026", "text": "3. The pump is choked", "bbox": {"x0": 203.69, "top": 533.148, "x1": 320.34, "bottom": 544.188}, "reading_order": 26, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP005:p0060:b0027", "text": "Clean the pump", "bbox": {"x0": 371.11, "top": 536.148, "x1": 448.865, "bottom": 547.188}, "reading_order": 27, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP005:p0060:b0028", "text": "The pump has no or", "bbox": {"x0": 90.384, "top": 541.308, "x1": 188.839, "bottom": 552.348}, "reading_order": 28, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP005:p0060:b0029", "text": "4. Suction line leaks", "bbox": {"x0": 203.69, "top": 553.068, "x1": 306.771, "bottom": 564.108}, "reading_order": 29, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP005:p0060:b0030", "text": "too low capacity", "bbox": {"x0": 90.384, "top": 554.988, "x1": 168.724, "bottom": 566.028}, "reading_order": 30, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP005:p0060:b0031", "text": "Find the leakage, repair the fault,", "bbox": {"x0": 371.11, "top": 559.788, "x1": 531.941, "bottom": 570.828}, "reading_order": 31, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP005:p0060:b0032", "text": "5. Pump takes air", "bbox": {"x0": 203.69, "top": 572.388, "x1": 294.473, "bottom": 583.428}, "reading_order": 32, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP005:p0060:b0033", "text": "non-return valve not submerged", "bbox": {"x0": 371.11, "top": 572.388, "x1": 527.216, "bottom": 583.428}, "reading_order": 33, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP005:p0060:b0034", "text": "Check data sheet Q/H curve and", "bbox": {"x0": 371.11, "top": 595.188, "x1": 530.793, "bottom": 606.228}, "reading_order": 34, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP005:p0060:b0035", "text": "6. Suction lift is too high", "bbox": {"x0": 203.69, "top": 601.548, "x1": 325.158, "bottom": 612.588}, "reading_order": 35, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP005:p0060:b0036", "text": "NPSH or contact DESMI", "bbox": {"x0": 371.11, "top": 613.788, "x1": 491.004, "bottom": 624.828}, "reading_order": 36, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP005:p0060:b0037", "text": "7. Pump and piping system", "bbox": {"x0": 203.69, "top": 628.308, "x1": 341.636, "bottom": 639.348}, "reading_order": 37, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP005:p0060:b0038", "text": "As 5", "bbox": {"x0": 371.11, "top": 638.058, "x1": 393.201, "bottom": 649.098}, "reading_order": 38, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP005:p0060:b0039", "text": "wrongly dimensioned", "bbox": {"x0": 221.09, "top": 641.898, "x1": 324.546, "bottom": 652.938}, "reading_order": 39, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP005:p0060:b0040", "text": "Insert orifice plate or check valve", "bbox": {"x0": 371.11, "top": 662.298, "x1": 531.378, "bottom": 673.338}, "reading_order": 40, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP005:p0060:b0041", "text": "1. Counter-pressure is too low", "bbox": {"x0": 203.69, "top": 666.138, "x1": 355.683, "bottom": 677.178}, "reading_order": 41, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP005:p0060:b0042", "text": "/ Contact DESMI", "bbox": {"x0": 371.11, "top": 675.978, "x1": 453.106, "bottom": 687.018}, "reading_order": 42, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP005:p0060:b0043", "text": "2. The liquid is heavier than", "bbox": {"x0": 203.69, "top": 690.378, "x1": 343.502, "bottom": 701.418}, "reading_order": 43, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP005:p0060:b0044", "text": "The pump uses too", "bbox": {"x0": 90.384, "top": 693.378, "x1": 184.71, "bottom": 704.418}, "reading_order": 44, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP005:p0060:b0045", "text": "Contact DESMI", "bbox": {"x0": 371.11, "top": 700.218, "x1": 446.988, "bottom": 711.258}, "reading_order": 45, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP005:p0060:b0046", "text": "water", "bbox": {"x0": 221.09, "top": 704.058, "x1": 248.028, "bottom": 715.098}, "reading_order": 46, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP005:p0060:b0047", "text": "much power", "bbox": {"x0": 90.384, "top": 707.058, "x1": 150.32, "bottom": 718.098}, "reading_order": 47, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP005:p0060:b0048", "text": "Dismantle the pump, remove the", "bbox": {"x0": 371.11, "top": 724.458, "x1": 530.196, "bottom": 735.498}, "reading_order": 48, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP005:p0060:b0049", "text": "3. Foreign body in pump", "bbox": {"x0": 203.69, "top": 728.298, "x1": 327.648, "bottom": 739.338}, "reading_order": 49, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP005:p0060:b0050", "text": "cause", "bbox": {"x0": 371.11, "top": 738.134, "x1": 400.532, "bottom": 749.174}, "reading_order": 50, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP005:p0060:b0051", "text": "DESMI Pumping Technology A/S", "bbox": {"x0": 463.9, "top": 776.196, "x1": 552.304, "bottom": 782.196}, "reading_order": 51, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP005:p0060:b0052", "text": "Tagholm 1", "bbox": {"x0": 524.02, "top": 783.156, "x1": 552.394, "bottom": 789.156}, "reading_order": 52, "block_type": "text_line